course: dictionary
lesson: 10269
title: One word, many places
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Top is a short word with many meanings. The meaning depends on the words around it. «The top shelf» means the highest shelf, and a top can also be a piece of clothing or a toy that spins.
explain: Ask yourself: what is being talked about? «Thunderstorm clouds reach so high that their tops are far below freezing, even in summer.» Here the tops are the highest parts of the clouds. Clouds have no lids, so top cannot mean a lid in this sentence.
explain: Sometimes top means the best or the highest rank. «South Africa accused Israel of genocide at the International Court of Justice, the UN's top court.» The top court is the highest court of the UN, not a piece of clothing or a toy.
explain: Other clues come from small phrases such as «on top of» or «from top to bottom». «A swing is fastest at the bottom and slowest at the top.» Top and bottom are opposites here, so top means the highest point of the swing.
fact: Top means the highest part of something, like the top of a hill.
fact: The top is also the upper surface or the lid, like a bottle top.
fact: A top is a piece of clothing for the upper body, like a T-shirt.
fact: A spinning top is a toy that spins on a point.
fact: To top something means to put something on it, or to be better than it.
fact: «Pollen from the feathery tassel on top must land on that silk or the kernel never grows.» Here top means the upper part of the corn plant.
fact: In a fraction, the top number is the numerator.
exercise: «A swing is fastest at the bottom and slowest at the top.» Where is the swing slowest? | Nowhere, it stays the same | At the bottom | In the middle | *At the top
exercise: «Show me the top mark you got in the test.» What does top mean in this sentence? | A piece of clothing | A spinning toy | *The best or highest | A lid
exercise: In the fraction 3/4, the top number is the numerator. Which number is the top number? | 1 | 34 | *3 | 4
exercise: Ella says top always means a shirt. Which sentence is she wrong about? | «She wore a red top.» | «He spun the top on the table.» | «Put the bottle top back on.» | *«The top of the hill was covered in snow.»
test: «Thunderstorm clouds reach so high that their tops are far below freezing.» What are the tops of the clouds? | Toys that spin | A piece of clothing for the clouds | The lids of the clouds | *The highest parts of the clouds
test: Leo says, «Let's top the pizza with cheese and ham.» What does top mean here? | To take it off the plate | To spin it on a point | To make it the best pizza ever made, which is the only meaning | *To put something on it
exam: Which word fits best in «She wore a bright blue ___ to school»? | window | table | *top | pencil
